      "headline": "NASA Finalizes Artemis II Moon Rocket Rollout to Launch Pad 39B",
      "description": "NASA initiated the rollout of the Artemis II Space Launch System rocket and Orion spacecraft to Launch Pad 39B at Kennedy Space Center, Florida, beginning at 8 p.m. EDT on March 19, 2026. This second rollout — following a February return to the Vehicle Assembly Building to address a helium flow issue in the interim cryogenic propulsion stage — targets a launch attempt no earlier than April 1, 2026. The four-person crew (Commander Reid Wiseman, Pilot Victor Glover, Mission Specialist Christina Koch, and CSA Mission Specialist Jeremy Hansen) simultaneously entered pre-launch quarantine.",
      "context": "Artemis II will be the first crewed mission beyond low Earth orbit since Apollo 17 in December 1972, sending four astronauts on a free-return trajectory around the Moon and back. The mission achieves multiple historic firsts: first woman, first person of color, and first non-American to reach the lunar vicinity. Successful execution validates the SLS-Orion crewed deep space architecture ahead of Artemis III, which will attempt the first crewed lunar landing since 1972 and anchor NASA's Moon-to-Mars exploration strategy.",
      "timeline": [
