      "headline": "Surgical Breakthrough: Critically Ill Patient Survives 48 Hours Without Lungs Using Groundbreaking Life-Support Technique",
      "description": "Surgeons at Northwestern University led by Dr. Ankit Bharat successfully kept a 33-year-old Missouri patient alive for 48 hours after surgically removing both of his irreversibly infected lungs, using a custom-engineered total artificial lung (TAL) system. The device oxygenated the blood, removed carbon dioxide, maintained stable circulation, and used tissue expanders to stabilize the heart in the empty chest cavity. Two days later, a donor became available and a double lung transplant was performed. More than two years later, the patient has resumed normal life with strong lung function. The case was published in Cell Press journal Med.",
      "context": "This represents the first documented case of a patient surviving bilateral pneumonectomy (both lungs removed) while bridged to a successful transplant using a total artificial lung system. The case challenges the conventional strategy of supportive waiting for ARDS patients whose lungs are irrecoverably damaged, providing molecular proof via transcriptomic analysis that some patients require transplant as the only viable path. If standardized, this approach could save young patients dying of catastrophic viral or infectious lung failure — a population for whom transplant has historically not been considered in acute settings.",
      "timeline": [
        {"type": "background", "date": "2023-03-01", "label": "A 33-year-old Missouri man develops flu-triggered ARDS with bacterial pneumonia; both lungs fail irreversibly; heart stops on arrival at Northwestern Memorial Hospital."},
        {"type": "escalation", "date": "2023-03-15", "label": "Surgeons decide to remove both infected lungs and deploy a custom total artificial lung system to stabilize the patient for transplant."},
        {"type": "event", "date": "2026-01-30", "label": "Northwestern Medicine publishes the case in Cell Press journal Med, including molecular proof of irreversible lung damage via single-cell transcriptomics."},
        {"type": "consequence", "date": "2026-03-18", "label": "Case receives global scientific coverage; Bharat advocates for standardizing artificial lung bridge-to-transplant protocols at more specialized centers."}
      ],
      "importance_score": 5,
      "category": "science",
      "region": "North America",
      "key_terms": [
