        {"term": "Bilateral Pneumonectomy", "definition": "Surgical removal of both lungs; historically fatal due to immediate cardiac failure; this case is the first documented survival using TAL bridge-to-transplant."},
        {"term": "ARDS (Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome)", "definition": "A severe, often fatal condition in which lung inflammation and infection overwhelm respiratory function; the underlying diagnosis in this case."},
        {"term": "Bridge-to-Transplant Strategy", "definition": "The clinical approach of using artificial organ support to stabilize a patient long enough for a donor organ to become available for transplantation."},
        {"term": "Single-Cell Transcriptomics", "definition": "Advanced genomic technique used to analyze gene expression at the individual cell level; used to provide molecular proof that the patient's lungs were beyond recovery."},
