        {"term": "Hydroxyl Megamaser", "definition": "An extremely bright natural radio emission produced when hydroxyl (OH) molecules in gas-rich, merging galaxies amplify radio waves, analogous to a laser but at radio wavelengths."},
        {"term": "Gigamaser", "definition": "A proposed classification tier for hydroxyl megamasers of extraordinary luminosity, first applied to HATLAS J142935.3–002836."},
        {"term": "Gravitational Lensing", "definition": "The bending of light by massive objects in space that amplifies distant signals; a foreground galaxy acted as a natural cosmic lens for this gigamaser detection."},
